<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!-- Projector is not sandboxed. It is distributed as a notarized Developer ID
     DMG and updates itself through Sparkle, whose installer entitlements already
     ruled out the Mac App Store - the only place a sandbox is required.

     The sandbox cost the workflow more than it protected: a dropped file granted
     only that file, so saving a project beside its media, writing Optimized Media
     and relinking moved files each needed a folder panel or a stored bookmark,
     and bookmarks broke between builds. Without it the app reads and writes
     wherever the user can.

     Hardened Runtime (required for notarization) is still on and needs no
     exceptions: nothing here records audio, uses the camera or JITs code.
     The Quick Look extension keeps its own sandbox; extensions require one. -->
<dict/>
</plist>
